```java
@Query("SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.email = :email") // entity + field
Optional<User> findByEmail(@Param("email") String email);

@Query("SELECT DISTINCT u FROM User u JOIN u.orders o") // navigate the field
List<User> withOrders();
```
JPQL uses the entity class `User` and the field `u.email`; the provider maps them to the real table and column.

```java
@Repository
public interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {

    // Join across a relationship
    @Query("SELECT o FROM Order o JOIN o.user u WHERE u.email = :email")
    List<Order> findByUserEmail(@Param("email") String email);

    // Aggregate
    @Query("SELECT COUNT(o) FROM Order o WHERE o.status = :status")
    long countByStatus(@Param("status") OrderStatus status);

    // JOIN FETCH solves N+1 by loading the collection in one query
    @Query("SELECT o FROM Order o JOIN FETCH o.lineItems WHERE o.id = :id")
    Optional<Order> findWithItems(@Param("id") Long id);

    // Constructor expression → DTO projection
    @Query("SELECT new com.example.dto.OrderSummary(o.id, o.total) FROM Order o")
    List<OrderSummary> summaries();
}
```

```java
@Transactional
public void rename(Long id, String name) {
    var user = userRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
    user.setName(name);
    userRepository.save(user); // redundant — already managed
}
```

```java
@Transactional
public void rename(Long id, String name) {
    var user = userRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow(); // managed
    user.setName(name); // change tracked automatically
    // no save() — UPDATE flushed at commit
}
```
If the entity were **detached** (loaded outside this transaction), you'd need `save()`/`merge()` to reattach it.

```java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    private final OrderRepository orderRepository;
    OrderService(OrderRepository r) { this.orderRepository = r; }

    @Transactional
    public void demo(Long orderId) {
        var first = orderRepository.findById(orderId).orElseThrow(); // SELECT
        var second = orderRepository.findById(orderId).orElseThrow(); // no SELECT (cached)
        System.out.println(first == second); // true — same managed object

        first.setStatus("SHIPPED"); // dirty checking → UPDATE at commit
    }
}
```

```java
@Transactional
public void update(Long id, String name) {
    User detached = loadFromCache(id); // from a previous tx — DETACHED
    detached.setName(name);
    // expecting dirty checking to flush this — it won't; entity isn't managed
}
```

```java
@Transactional
public void update(Long id, String name) {
    User detached = loadFromCache(id);
    detached.setName(name);
    userRepository.save(detached); // detached → merge: SELECT then UPDATE
}
```
`save()` on a detached entity runs a SELECT first, so it's not a simple UPDATE — keep using the returned managed instance.

```java
@Service
public class ProductService {
    private final ProductRepository repo;
    ProductService(ProductRepository r) { this.repo = r; }

    @Transactional
    public void lifecycle() {
        var product = new Product(null, "Laptop", 1200.0); // TRANSIENT
        repo.save(product);          // → MANAGED (id assigned)
        product.setPrice(1100.0);    // tracked, no save() needed
    }                                 // tx ends → product is DETACHED

    @Transactional
    public void delete(Long id) {
        var product = repo.findById(id).orElseThrow(); // MANAGED
        repo.delete(product);        // REMOVED — DELETE at commit
        System.out.println(product.getId()); // still readable in memory
    }
}
```
